{"id": "EUVD-2026-90573", "enisaUuid": "ff217dd5-5ae7-3d58-b86d-e9cf79d30c39", "description": "The Duplicate Post plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Stored Cross-Site Scripting via the 'noti_token' parameter in all versions up to, and including, 1.5.6 due to insufficient input sanitization and output escaping. This makes it possible for authenticated attackers, with subscriber-level access and above, to inject arbitrary web scripts in pages that will execute whenever a user accesses an injected page. This requires that the site owner has enabled the plugin's User Level Permissions for the Subscriber role, as this grants access to the i_saw_this_noti AJAX branch needed to deliver the payload.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T08:28:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T14:13:50", "baseScore": 6.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://www.wordfence.com/threat-intel/vulnerabilities/id/c475c51e-f01d-4698-822f-5b8df999bf6d?source=cve", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/copy-delete-posts/tags/1.5.6/menu/notifications.php#L53", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/copy-delete-posts/tags/1.5.6/menu/notifications.php#L84", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/copy-delete-posts/tags/1.5.6/post/handler.php#L1598", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/copy-delete-posts/tags/1.5.6/post/handler.php#L1601", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/copy-delete-posts/tags/1.5.6/post/handler.php#L15", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/changeset?reponame=&new=3709767%40copy-delete-posts%2Ftags%2F1.5.7&old=3652254%40copy-delete-posts%2Ftags%2F1.5.6", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/changeset/3709767/copy-delete-posts/trunk/menu/notifications.php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89424", "GHSA-mjxg-mhjq-2vx5"], "assigner": "Wordfence", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8f042f4b-5bc1-3562-b620-fc2b482a09c6", "product": {"name": "Duplicate Post", "vendor": {"name": "copydeletep